menu "DHCP server"

    config USE_OWN_DHCPS
        bool "Use the vendored DHCP server instead of ESP-IDF's"
        default y
        help
            Runs main/dhcps/vendored_dhcps.c, a copy of ESP-IDF's DHCP server,
            so it can be extended (static leases). The vendored copy and IDF's
            define the same dhcps_* symbols, so they cannot both be compiled:
            enabling this REQUIRES "Component config -> LWIP -> DHCPS" to be
            disabled. With CONFIG_LWIP_DHCPS=y the build fails at link time with
            duplicate dhcps_new/dhcps_start definitions.

            Turning this off is the rollback path: it restores IDF's server and
            the esp_netif-based integration, with no other code changes.

            Note the IDF Kconfig settings under DHCPS (max stations, lease unit,
            hostname reporting) disappear when that option is off; the vendored
            copy carries matching defaults in dhcps/vendored_dhcps_config.h.

endmenu

menu "Onboard RGB LED"

    config LED_RGB_TEST_COLORS
        bool "Diagnostic: drive R/G/B on the listed GPIOs to find the LED pin"
        default n
        help
            Instead of sending black, send red to the first GPIO in the list,
            green to the second and blue to the third. Whichever colour appears
            identifies the pin that actually carries the LED. Turn this off and
            narrow LED_RGB_GPIO_LIST to that one pin afterwards.

    config LED_RGB_GPIO_LIST
        string "WS2812 data GPIOs to drive black at boot (comma-separated)"
        default "48,38,47"
        help
            A WS2812 latches its last colour, so a freshly flashed image leaves
            the onboard RGB LED showing whatever the previous firmware wrote
            there. This firmware never drives the LED, so it does not clear on
            its own. Each GPIO listed here is sent a single black pixel once at
            boot, which switches off whichever of them carries the LED.

            Which pin carries the LED varies between board revisions of the
            ESP32-S3 N16R8 family, hence the list. Set to "" to leave the LED
            under whatever the previous firmware left it at, or to a single
            GPIO once you know which one works.

            Do not list GPIO 33-37: those carry the octal PSRAM.

endmenu
